{"name":"Dry Season","hex":"#d4cecd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dry season","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any season in which little rain falls; used especially in the tropics where it alternates with the rainy season."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry_season"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dry season","blocks":[{"text":"The dry season is a yearly period of low rainfall, especially in the tropics. The weather in the tropics is dominated by the tropical rain belt, which moves from the northern to the southern tropics and back over the course of the year. The temperate counterpart to the tropical dry season is summer or winter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Long_shadow_of_a_dead_tree_with_its_branches_on_the_dry_fields_of_Laos_-_landscape.jpg/330px-Long_shadow_of_a_dead_tree_with_its_branches_on_the_dry_fields_of_Laos_-_landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dry_season","wikidata":"Q146575"},{"title":"Dry Season (2006 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Dry Season Arabic: دارات, romanized: Daratt; French: Saison sèche) is a 2006 film by Chadian director Mahamat Saleh Haroun."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Daratt_%28movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dry_Season_(2006_film)","wikidata":"Q689067"},{"title":"Season","blocks":[{"text":"A season is a division of the year based on changes in weather, ecology, and the number of daylight hours in a given region. On Earth, seasons are the result of the axial parallelism of Earth's tilted orbit around the Sun. In temperate and polar regions, the seasons are marked by changes in the intensity of sunlight that reaches the Earth's surface, variations of which may cause animals to undergo hibernation or to migrate, and plants to be dormant. Various cultures define the number and nature of seasons based on regional variations, and as such there are a number of both modern and historical definitions of the seasons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/ChangingSeasons_NH_01.png/330px-ChangingSeasons_NH_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Season","wikidata":"Q24384"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/33/Daratt_%28movie_poster%29.jpg/250px-Daratt_%28movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Daratt_%28movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/33/Daratt_%28movie_poster%29.jpg/250px-Daratt_%28movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaratt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/North_season.jpg/500px-North_season.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/North_season.jpg/1280px-North_season.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/North_season.jpg/500px-North_season.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Axial parallelism is a characteristic of the Earth (and most other orbiting bodies in space) in which the direction of the axis remains parallel to itself throughout its orbit.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorth_season.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Earth-lighting-summer-solstice_EN_-_corrected.png/120px-Earth-lighting-summer-solstice_EN_-_corrected.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Earth-lighting-summer-solstice_EN_-_corrected.png/250px-Earth-lighting-summer-solstice_EN_-_corrected.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Earth-lighting-summer-solstice_EN_-_corrected.png/120px-Earth-lighting-summer-solstice_EN_-_corrected.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth-lighting-summer-solstice_EN_-_corrected.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/120px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/250px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/120px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Earth_seasons_2021-2022.jpg/120px-Earth_seasons_2021-2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Earth_seasons_2021-2022.jpg/250px-Earth_seasons_2021-2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Earth_seasons_2021-2022.jpg/120px-Earth_seasons_2021-2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars